    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nCannot assign lua functions/closures to a \"func\" ('completefunc', 'tagfun', ...) or \"expr\" ('foldexpr', 'indentexpr', ...) option.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n- Store \"func\" option value as `Callback` instead of string.\r\n- Delete oceans of copy-pasted code.\r\n- LuaRef in a RPC response is now a human-readable hint `\"<Lua N: file:line>\"` (like what `:map` shows) instead of `nil`.\r\n- Note: `man.vim` still uses `v:lua` string, bc it's a vimscript ftplugin.\r\n\r\nRelated:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/25672\r\n\r\n\r\nsupersedes https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/31280\r\ncloses https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/18132\r\nwork towards https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/18997",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-31T22:01:52Z",
